# Origin of the kf_backend Express server (Render in production, localhost in dev).
# No trailing slash, and no /api suffix — the client appends /api itself, and
# uses this same origin for the Socket.io connection used by the chat widget.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000

# OPTIONAL. Origin of an image-resizing proxy, no trailing slash and no path —
# e.g. https://cdn.kftechsolutions.com. Nothing needs this to work.
#
# Left unset (the default, and what dev uses), photos load from their source
# with that source's own sizing parameters applied, so a full-resolution
# original is never shipped. Set it and photos are served right-sized,
# AVIF/WebP-negotiated and edge-cached from your own domain instead.
# VITE_IMAGE_CDN=

# Absolute origin of the deployed site, no trailing slash — e.g. https://kftechsolutions.com
#
# Canonical URLs, hreflang alternates, Open Graph URLs, JSON-LD and sitemap.xml
# all need an absolute origin, and a wrong one is worse than none: it tells
# Google the real page lives somewhere else. Leave it unset and the build skips
# per-route SEO tags (with a warning) rather than guessing.
#
# Unset in dev: the site falls back to the origin it is served from.
VITE_SITE_URL=
